inating blue hues were replaced  with reds and oranges  and you would spend the game building up  to this epic conclusion  the infamous suicide mission there it is  the collector base  mass effect 2 was an enormous success a  critical darling and recipient of  numerous awards including the bafta for  best game  it quickly earned spots on lists of best  games of all time and fans absolutely  adored it  the pressure for the third part of the  trilogy was immense  could mass effect 3 marry the two very  different tones of me1 and 2 together  as well as make good on the countless  decisions players had made along the way  to create a conclusion and sequel  befitting of both  the answer to that is in some cases yes  but in other cases no mass effect 3 was  still very much an action game but it  did mark the return  for some of the series early rpg  elements the leveling system was much  more in-depth than twos and weapon and  character customization were taken to  further lengths  it was still a little light on  exploration but with the impending  threat of the reapers coming to destroy  the galaxy  would there really be that much time for  exploring probably not  so instead bioware took another crack at  the combat  and managed to squeeze in the last  puzzle piece that was always missing  melee attacks for the first time in this  series combat just kind of came together  and worked beautifully it didn't feel  janky like mass effect 1 and felt more  cohesive than mass effect 2  it emphasized combos let you grab  enemies from behind cover and added new  powers  the place it really shone was in the  game's pve multiplayer mode which is  still  actually active today the combat was the  best it had ever been and narratively  all the dominoes that had been set up  over the course of six years  were finally starting to fall decisions  came full circle like the raknai queen  on novaria and captain kirahi's fate on  vermeyer  players had vastly different experiences  with mass e